        <mxCell id="pb1_bniJC4KUjT1g9-vP-14" value="The core metrics I want:&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Weekly Threshold Volume&lt;/b&gt;: total kilometer or time spent strickly between my LT1 (aerobic threshold) and LT2 (anaerobic threshold)&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Autonomic Recovery Score&lt;/b&gt;: A custom overlay tracking your 7-day rolling waking HRV against your total threshold volume to flag when the high-volume system is overloading your nervous system.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;ADD MORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="290" y="560" width="450" height="170" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="pb1_bniJC4KUjT1g9-vP-15" value="The graphs I want:&lt;div&gt;&lt;ol&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Intensity Distribution Histogram&lt;/b&gt;: A classic 3-zone pyramidal vs. polarized chart showing exactly how much time is spent below LT1 (Zone 1), between LT1 and LT2 (Zone 2 - the Norwegian sweet spot), and above LT2 (Zone 3).&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Cardiovascular Drift Tracker&lt;/b&gt;: A scatter plot analyzing long, steady workouts to see if your heart rate spikes relative to a stable pace over time, proving if your base aerobic engine is truly optimized.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;Per ogni corsa, quanto sono in percentuale rispetto all&#39;HR Max&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;b&gt;ADD MORE&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ol&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" parent="1" vertex="1">
